WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.672
I had a non traditional
path to Wall Street.

00:00:03.672 --> 00:00:06.621
But what's cool that wasn't
a typical feeder school.

00:00:06.621 --> 00:00:09.904
And at the last second I gave
consideration to doing the two

00:00:09.904 --> 00:00:12.049
year analyst program on Wall Street.

00:00:12.049 --> 00:00:16.361
By frankly, I had a little bit of
success and unexpected success and

00:00:16.361 --> 00:00:20.524
fell in love with Wall Street
decided to stay in the industry, and

00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:22.581
progressed through my career.

00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:27.298
Why I gravitated to Stanford was really
around the innovation, disruption,

00:00:27.298 --> 00:00:32.085
some of the the technology aspects and
how the world is going to be different 10,

00:00:32.085 --> 00:00:33.816
20, 30 years from now.

00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:36.408
In the belief that you need
this sort of background and

00:00:36.408 --> 00:00:40.166
understanding all of these currents to
be a successful leader in the future.

00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.245
Silicon Value in my opinion has
woken up to this industry and

00:00:43.245 --> 00:00:44.484
wanting to disrupt it.

00:00:44.484 --> 00:00:47.119
I think financial institutions
really need to figure out and

00:00:47.119 --> 00:00:48.936
I think they're doing it in a lot of ways.

00:00:48.936 --> 00:00:54.312
How do I take this underlying industry if
you rely on the disruption side seriously.

00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:55.959
How do I figure out how to work with them?

00:00:55.959 --> 00:00:58.073
How do I figure out how
to partner with them?

00:00:58.073 --> 00:01:00.103
Being out at Stanford,
sitting in Palo Alto,

00:01:00.103 --> 00:01:02.082
meeting with all
the venture capital funds,

00:01:02.082 --> 00:01:05.637
seeing what the professors are talking
about, what the students are learning.

00:01:05.637 --> 00:01:11.433
It made me realize that innovation and
disruption is really here to stay.

00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:13.280
You can't compete with it.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:23.280
[MUSIC]

